25 Section 1. Section 53G-7-1202 is amended to read:
26 53G-7-1202. School community councils -- Duties -- Composition -- Election procedures and
selection of members.
25 (1) As used in this section:
26 (a) "Digital citizenship" means the norms of appropriate, responsible, and healthy behavior related to
technology use, including digital literacy, ethics, etiquette, and security.
29 (b) "Educator" means the same as that term is defined in Section 53E-6-102.
30 (c)
(i) "Parent member" means a member of a school community council who is a parent of a student who:
32 (A) is attending the school; or
33 (B) will be enrolled at the school during the parent's term of office.
34 (ii) "Parent member" may not include an educator who is employed at the school.
35 (d) "Safety principles" means safety principles that, when incorporated into programs and resources,
impact academic achievement by strengthening a safe and wholesome learning environment,
including continual efforts for safe technology utilization and digital citizenship.
39 (e) "School community council" means a council established at a district school in accordance with this
section.
41 (f) "School employee member" means a member of a school community council who is a person
employed at the school by the school or school district, including the principal.
44 (g) "School LAND Trust Program money" means money allocated to a school [pursuant to] in
accordance with Section 53F-2-404.
